# Kotlin / Jetpack Compose (Android)

Caps: soft **250** / hard **400** lines per file; functions **≤50** lines. Screens and component dumps must split before hard cap.

## Principles (Context7 / Android + Compose rules)

- **State hoisting**: stateful screen + stateless content; pass values + lambdas, not `State<T>` holders
- Hoist shared UI state to the nearest common ancestor; give child defaults (`rememberLazyListState()`) when reusable
- Side effects only via `LaunchedEffect` / `DisposableEffect` / `rememberCoroutineScope` — composables stay idempotent
- Cache expensive work with `remember`; stabilize lazy items with keys; use `derivedStateOf` / deferred reads to limit recomposition
- Composable params: required first, then `modifier: Modifier = Modifier`, then other optionals, trailing `@Composable` content last
- Apply the `modifier` only on the root layout node; children get fresh `Modifier`
- Inject ViewModels as parameters with defaults (`viewModel: X = hiltViewModel()`), not hidden `viewModel()` calls inside the body

## Kotlin conventions

- Official style: `camelCase` functions/properties; file name = single public type, or UpperCamelCase describing contents (no `Util`)
- Keep related declarations in one file only while size stays reasonable; otherwise split by feature
- Prefer `val`, data classes, sealed hierarchies, and explicit visibility
- Coroutines for async; never block the main thread

## Structure

- `screens/<feature>/` for UI + ViewModels; `vault/`, `network/`, `theme/` for domain/shared
- Extract list items, dialogs, and sections into private or file-local composables when the screen nears soft cap

```kotlin
// ✅ Hoisted, testable content
@Composable
fun HelloScreen(vm: HelloVm = hiltViewModel()) {
    val name by vm.name.collectAsState()
    HelloContent(name = name, onNameChange = vm::onNameChange)
}

@Composable
fun HelloContent(name: String, onNameChange: (String) -> Unit, modifier: Modifier = Modifier) { /* ... */ }
```
